1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:01,480
At the equator,

2
00:00:01,480 --> 00:00:02,491
the ground moves at

3
00:00:02,491 --> 00:00:05,736
1,670 km/h.

4
00:00:06,936 --> 00:00:08,260
Now stop the Earth.

5
00:00:08,260 --> 00:00:08,720
Instantly.

6
00:00:08,720 --> 00:00:10,100
The ground stops.

7
00:00:10,100 --> 00:00:10,695
You don't.

8
00:00:11,695 --> 00:00:12,720
You keep going east

9
00:00:12,720 --> 00:00:14,260
at the same speed.

10
00:00:14,260 --> 00:00:15,262
So does the air.

11
00:00:16,262 --> 00:00:16,940
That's a wind

12
00:00:16,940 --> 00:00:18,700
about 4 times faster

13
00:00:18,700 --> 00:00:20,140
than the strongest gust

14
00:00:20,140 --> 00:00:21,315
ever recorded.

15
00:00:22,415 --> 00:00:24,340
The oceans keep going too.

16
00:00:24,340 --> 00:00:25,664
Straight over the coasts.

17
00:00:26,764 --> 00:00:27,300
Fine.

18
00:00:27,300 --> 00:00:29,180
Let's stop it slowly instead.

19
00:00:29,180 --> 00:00:30,201
Over a few years.

20
00:00:31,201 --> 00:00:33,260
Spinning makes Earth bulge.

21
00:00:33,260 --> 00:00:33,777
The poles are

22
00:00:33,777 --> 00:00:35,400
21 km closer

23
00:00:35,400 --> 00:00:36,160
to the centre

24
00:00:36,160 --> 00:00:37,566
than the equator.

25
00:00:38,566 --> 00:00:39,680
Without the spin,

26
00:00:39,680 --> 00:00:40,620
the oceans slide

27
00:00:40,620 --> 00:00:41,920
to the poles.

28
00:00:41,920 --> 00:00:43,520
Two polar oceans,

29
00:00:43,520 --> 00:00:44,500
one belt of land

30
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:45,352
around the middle.

31
00:00:46,352 --> 00:00:48,100
Everything north of Spain?

32
00:00:48,100 --> 00:00:48,916
Underwater.

33
00:00:50,016 --> 00:00:50,620
And one day

34
00:00:50,620 --> 00:00:52,240
lasts a whole year.

35
00:00:52,240 --> 00:00:53,760
6 months of daylight.

36
00:00:53,760 --> 00:00:55,202
Then 6 months of night.

37
00:00:56,102 --> 00:00:57,620
Long enough to bake the land

38
00:00:57,620 --> 00:00:59,382
past 100 degrees.

39
00:01:00,482 --> 00:01:02,120
Here's the real part.

40
00:01:02,120 --> 00:01:03,840
Earth is slowing down.

41
00:01:03,840 --> 00:01:04,980
Every century,

42
00:01:04,980 --> 00:01:05,882
the day gets about

43
00:01:05,882 --> 00:01:08,180
1.8 thousandths of a second

44
00:01:08,180 --> 00:01:08,679
longer.

45
00:01:09,679 --> 00:01:10,480
At that rate,

46
00:01:10,480 --> 00:01:11,580
it takes Earth about

47
00:01:11,580 --> 00:01:13,100
200 million years

48
00:01:13,100 --> 00:01:15,171
to add one extra hour.

49
00:01:16,271 --> 00:01:17,400
So relax.

50
00:01:17,400 --> 00:01:18,680
Earth won't stop.

51
00:01:18,680 --> 00:01:20,154
It's just taking its time.

